# The build image installs packages and copies nothing, so it needs no context
# at all.  Without this, `docker build .` tars the entire repository into the
# daemon first -- on the author's machine that is a ~1 GB .git plus a ~1.5 GB
# kernel clone under build/, which is slow at best and on Docker's legacy
# builder fails outright with "Can't add file .../.git to tar: io: read/write
# on closed pipe".
#
# If the Dockerfile ever gains a COPY, un-ignore exactly what it copies.
*
!Dockerfile
